Aurora 2026-10-25: build Shairport Sync 4.3.7's AirPlay 2 mode against FFmpeg 9 (Fedora 45).

Why: has_fltp_capable_aac_decoder() reads AVCodec.sample_fmts to check that the AAC decoder
can output float planar audio, which buffered (AAC) AirPlay 2 streams need. FFmpeg 7.1
deprecated that field in favour of avcodec_get_supported_config(), and FFmpeg 9
(libavcodec 63, Fedora 45's libavcodec-free 9.0) removed it, so the build fails with
"'AVCodec' has no member named 'sample_fmts'".

What: use avcodec_get_supported_config(NULL, codec, AV_CODEC_CONFIG_SAMPLE_FORMAT, ...) when
libavcodec is 61.13.100 or newer; older libavcodec keeps the original loop. The answer is the
same list FFmpeg used to publish in sample_fmts. This is the only FFmpeg 9 break in 4.3.7.

--- a/shairport.c
+++ b/shairport.c
@@ -160,6 +160,20 @@
   int has_capability = 0;
   const AVCodec *codec = avcodec_find_decoder(AV_CODEC_ID_AAC);
   if (codec != NULL) {
+#if LIBAVCODEC_VERSION_INT >= AV_VERSION_INT(61, 13, 100)
+    // FFmpeg 7.1 (libavcodec 61.13.100) replaced AVCodec.sample_fmts with
+    // avcodec_get_supported_config(), and FFmpeg 9 (libavcodec 63) removed the field.
+    const enum AVSampleFormat *p = NULL;
+    int n = 0;
+    if ((avcodec_get_supported_config(NULL, codec, AV_CODEC_CONFIG_SAMPLE_FORMAT, 0,
+                                      (const void **)&p, &n) >= 0) &&
+        (p != NULL)) {
+      int i;
+      for (i = 0; (has_capability == 0) && (i < n); i++)
+        if (p[i] == AV_SAMPLE_FMT_FLTP)
+          has_capability = 1;
+    }
+#else
     const enum AVSampleFormat *p = codec->sample_fmts;
     if (p != NULL) {
       while ((has_capability == 0) && (*p != AV_SAMPLE_FMT_NONE)) {
@@ -168,6 +182,7 @@
         p++;
       }
     }
+#endif
   }
   return has_capability;
 }
